{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0168Dn5wePU6fuzBYjx5GZ8M","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN.md — SOS Implementation Plan (handoff to the implementer)\n2\t\n3\tYou are the implementation agent. This file is your **entire** brief — the planning\n4\tsession that produced it is gone. Implement 10 SOS cards in\n5\t`cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` (collector numbers **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201,\n6\t226, 245, 257**), making **additive** engine changes as needed, and write your own\n7\ttests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n8\t\n9\t## Hard constraints (from AGENTS.md — do not violate)\n10\t\n11\t1. **Card location invariant** — each card's class stays in\n12\t   `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. The class names are fixed (already in the\n13\t   stubs): `TheDawningArchaic`, `TogetherAsOne`,\n14\t   `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares`, `ManaSculpt`, `RalZarekGuestLecturer`,\n15\t   `ImprovisationCapstone`, `LoreholdTheHistorian`, `SilverquillTheDisputant`,\n16\t   `WitherbloomTheBalancer`, `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex`.\n17\t2. **Read-only tests** — never edit/add/delete anything in `engine_tests/`, and\n18\t   never edit existing `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`. Read them as examples only.\n19\t3. **Additive-only engine** — you MAY add files/methods/classes/helpers in\n20\t   `engine/` and MAY modify the **bodies** of existing functions. You MUST NOT\n21\t   rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/`. No\n22\t   refactoring. After every engine change, run `pytest` and confirm\n23\t   `engine_tests/` and all FDN tests still pass.\n24\t4. Rules questions → grep `RULEBOOK.txt` (see `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## Engine facts you must know (verified against the source)\n29\t\n30\tThese are the seams the per-card plans rely on. File references are current.\n31\t\n32\t**Card hooks** (`engine/card.py`, base `CardImpl`): `can_cast(game)->bool`,\n33\t`cost_reduction(game)->int` (generic-only reduction; clamped `0..generic`),\n34\t`on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)`, `get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]`,\n35\t`register_triggers(game)`, `register_replacement_effects(game)`,\n36\t`get_activated_abilities()->list[ActivatedAbility]`, `get_modes()`. Subclasses:\n37\t`Creature` (`base_power/base_toughness`, `modified_power/modified_toughness`,\n38\t`power`/`toughness` properties = modified + `plus_one_counters` − `minus_one_counters`,\n39\t`_reset_characteristics()`), `Instant`, `Sorcery`, `Enchantment`, `Aura`,\n40\t`Artifact`, `ArtifactCreature`, `Planeswalker` (`starting_loyalty`, `loyalty`,\n41\t`get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]`), `Land` (`can_cast` returns\n42\t`False`, `get_mana_abilities()->list[ManaAbility]`).\n43\t\n44\t**Targeting** (`engine/types.py`): `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)`.\n45\tThe cast pipeline calls `player.choose_target` once per spec and stores results, in\n46\torder, on `card.chosen_targets`. At resolution read them back. The FDN convention\n47\t(see `cards/fdn/fdn_48`, `fdn_187`) is a module helper:\n48\t```python\n49\tdef _get_chosen_target(card, game):\n50\t    chosen = getattr(card, \"chosen_targets\", None)\n51\t    if chosen: return chosen[0]\n52\t    return getattr(card, \"_resolve_target\", None)  # test backdoor\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\t**Casting** (`engine/casting.py`):\n56\t- `cast_spell(game, player, card)` — full pipeline: timing → `can_cast` → hand →\n57\t  stack → targets → protection → cost reduction → pay → records\n58\t  `card.colors_spent = list(pool.last_payment_colors)` → `on_cast` → push\n59\t  `StackObject`. **Does NOT currently fire a spell-cast event** (gap #2) and **does\n60\t  NOT record total mana spent** (gap #5).\n61\t- `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` — casts with **no timing and no\n62\t  mana**, goes on the stack normally, can be countered. Used by Etali (`fdn_194`).\n63\t- `_resolve_spell(...)` — calls `card.on_resolve`, then moves permanents →\n64\t  battlefield, instants/sorceries → graveyard (no replacement consulted on this\n65\t  move; see gap #4).\n66\t- `get_cost_reduction(...)` only queries the card's own `cost_reduction` (gap #8).\n67\t- `is_sorcery_speed(game, player)` exists. `ManaCost.cmc` = generic + pips + hybrids\n68\t  (X counts as 0); `card.mana_cost.cmc` is a card's mana value.\n69\t\n70\t**Zones** (`engine/zones.py`): `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *,\n71\treplacement_event=None)`. Replacement effects are consulted **only when\n72\t`replacement_event` is given AND `from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`**. On ETB it fires\n73\t`EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` **before** calling the card's `register_triggers`\n74\t/ `register_replacement_effects` (so a permanent's own ETB trigger does NOT catch\n75\tits own entry — do \"when this enters\" work in `on_resolve` instead, like\n76\t`fdn_157`/`fdn_205`). On leaving the battlefield it fires LTB / CreatureDies then\n77\tunregisters the card's triggers/replacements.\n78\t\n79\t**Helpers** (`engine/game.py`): `draw_card(game, player)` (increments\n80\t`player.cards_drawn_this_turn`, fires `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`),\n81\t`discard(game, player, card)`, `create_token(game, player, token)`,\n82\t`destroy(game, permanent)`, `exile(game, obj)`, `deal_damage(game, src, tgt, amt)`,\n83\t`add_counter(game, permanent, counter_type, amount)` (supports `\"loyalty\"`,\n84\t`\"+1/+1\"`), `sacrifice(game, player, permanent)`.\n85\t\n86\t**Triggers** (`engine/triggers.py`): `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition,\n87\teffect, source, controller)`. `condition(game, event)->bool`; `effect(game)->None`\n88\t— **the effect does NOT receive the event**. To pass data from condition to effect,\n89\tuse the closure-queue pattern from `cards/fdn/fdn_141` (condition appends to a\n90\t`deque`, returns `True`; effect `popleft()`s it). `fire_event` matches by\n91\t`isinstance(event, event_type)` (subclass-aware), orders APNAP, pushes a\n92\t`StackObject` per match. `unregister(source)` removes all triggers whose `source`\n93\tis that object (identity) — use for one-shot delayed triggers.\n94\t\n95\t**Events** (`engine/events.py`): already-defined event classes you will use:\n96\t`EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent, controller, ...)`,\n97\t`DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card)`,\n98\t`SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)` (defined; **never\n99\tfired** — gap #2), `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)` (defined; **never\n100\tfired** — gap #1), `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` (fired each upkeep, **no\n101\tplayer field** — a condition must read `game.active_player`),\n102\t`CreatureDiesTriggeredEvent`. Replacement events:\n103\t`MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination, controller, owner, prevented)` with\n104\tsubclasses `CreatureDiesReplacementEvent(creature)`,\n105\t`PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent(permanent)`, `SacrificeReplacementEvent`;\n106\t`.card` property resolves on the subclass. Pattern reference: `cards/fdn/fdn_244`.\n107\t\n108\t**Abilities** (`engine/abilities.py`): `activate_ability(game, player, ability)`\n109\twhere `ability` is `ActivatedAbilityInstance(source, controller, cost, effect,\n110\tis_mana_ability, description)` or `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source, controller,\n111\tloyalty_cost, effect, description)`. Loyalty: sorcery-speed only, once/turn (keyed\n112\ton `object_id`+`turn_number`), adjusts `source.loyalty`, pushes `effect` to the\n113\tstack. `tap_cost(game, source)` taps if untapped. There is **no** auto-bridge from\n114\t`LoyaltyAbility` (the dataclass returned by `get_loyalty_abilities`) to\n115\t`LoyaltyAbilityInstance`; in tests, build the instance yourself from the\n116\tdataclass's `loyalty_cost`/`effect` and call `activate_ability`, or construct a\n117\t`LoyaltyAbilityInstance` directly.\n118\t\n119\t**Mana** (`engine/mana.py`): `pool.add(type, n)`, `pool.pay(cost)`,\n120\t`pool.can_pay(cost)`, `pool.last_payment_colors` (sorted distinct `Color`s spent on\n121\tthe most recent `pay`, colorless excluded). `ManaType` includes `COLORLESS`.\n122\t\n123\t**Turn loop** (`engine/turn.py` `run_turn`): fires only\n124\t`BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` (upkeep). Main phases are `(phase, None)` and\n125\tcurrently fire **no** begin-of-main event (gap #3). Combat steps dispatch to\n126\t`engine/combat.py`. Cleanup runs `effect_manager.remove_expired` + `apply_all`,\n127\tclears damage/combat flags, empties mana.\n128\t\n129\t**SBAs** (`engine/state_based_actions.py` `check_state_based_actions`): life≤0,\n130\ttoughness≤0, lethal damage, empty-library draw, legend rule, tokens off battlefield,\n131\tunattached auras, counter annihilation. **No planeswalker-0-loyalty check** (gap #6).\n132\t\n133\t**Continuous effects** (`engine/continuous_effects.py`):\n134\t`ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)`;\n135\t`Layer.{COPY,CONTROL,TEXT,TYPE,COLOR,ABILITY,POWER_TOUGHNESS}`,\n136\t`SubLayer.{CHARACTERISTIC_DEFINING,SET_PT,MODIFY_PT,COUNTERS}`,\n137\t`DURATION_PERMANENT=-1`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0`. `effect_manager.add(effect)`.\n138\t`apply_all` first calls each battlefield object's `_reset_characteristics()` then\n139\tre-applies effects in layer/timestamp order (so granted types/keywords/P-T must be\n140\tmodeled as registered effects, or restored in an overridden\n141\t`_reset_characteristics`, or they get wiped). EOT +X/+X pattern: `cards/fdn/fdn_6`.\n142\t\n143\t**Custom keywords are behavioral, not enum values.** `engine/types.py` `Keyword`\n144\thas only evergreen flags (FLYING, HASTE, VIGILANCE, DEATHTOUCH, REACH, TRAMPLE,\n145\tPROWESS, WARD, …). **Converge, Prepared, Paradigm, Miracle, Casualty, Affinity do\n146\tNOT exist as `Keyword` values and you do NOT need to add them** — implement them as\n147\tbehavior (cost reduction / triggers / on_resolve). Only set the evergreen keywords\n148\t(Reach, Flying, Haste, Vigilance, Deathtouch) via the `Keyword` flag. The FDN\n149\treferences confirm this (`fdn_6` Affinity, `fdn_205` Converge use no enum keyword).\n150\t\n151\t**Test helpers** (`test_utils.py`): `create_game(deck1, deck2, *, scripts=(s1,s2),\n152\tplayer1_life, player2_life)` (players are `DeterministicPlayer`s);\n153\t`set_board_state(game, idx, *, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana=)` —\n154\t**note there is NO `library=` or `exile=` parameter**: to seed those zones, mutate\n155\t`game.players[i].zones[Zone.LIBRARY]` / `[Zone.EXILE]` directly with `.add(card)`;\n156\t`cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=)` (scripts targets, casts, resolves the whole\n157\tstack); `advance_to_phase(game, phase, step=None)`; `declare_attackers(game,\n158\t[names])` (calls `declare_attackers_step` then leaves triggers on the stack — you\n159\tmust resolve them, e.g. `from engine.stack import priority_loop; priority_loop(game)`\n160\tor pop manually); `declare_blockers`. `DeterministicPlayer._script` is a `deque`;\n161\tscripted answers feed `choose`, `choose_target`, `choose_yes_no`, `choose_card`,\n162\t`assign_damage_order` in pop order. Reset object ids between tests if needed with\n163\t`GameObject.reset_id_counter()`.\n164\t\n165\t---\n166\t\n167\t## SECTION 1 — Engine gaps table\n168\t\n169\tPrefer the *smallest* additive change. All eight are independent and small. Make\n170\tthem first (see Section 3), then verify `engine_tests/` + FDN tests are green.\n171\t\n172\t| # | Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n173\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n174\t| 1 | \"Whenever ~ attacks\" triggers fire | In `declare_attackers_step`, after `attacker.is_attacking = True` and tapping, call `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))` for each declared attacker (import the event). | `engine/combat.py` `declare_attackers_step`; event already in `engine/events.py` | sos_1 |\n175\t| 2 | \"Whenever you cast …\" / casualty triggers fire | At the end of `cast_spell` (after the `StackObject` is pushed) fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player)`. Do the same at the end of `cast_spell_free`. (Copies via `copy_spell` do NOT go through these, so no recursion.) | `engine/casting.py`; event already in `engine/events.py` | sos_226, sos_257 |\n176\t| 3 | \"At the beginning of your … main phase\" triggers | Add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=None, is_first=False)` to `engine/events.py`. In `engine/turn.py` `run_turn`, add a branch: when `game.phase in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None`, fire it (before `priority_loop`) with `player=game.active_player`, `is_first=(game.phase == Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN)`. | `engine/events.py` + `engine/turn.py` | sos_57, sos_120 |\n177\t| 4 | \"If it would go to your graveyard, exile it instead\" (for a resolving spell) | In `_resolve_spell`, the instant/sorcery branch: if `getattr(card, \"_exile_on_resolve\", False)` is set, `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.EXILE)` instead of to graveyard. | `engine/casting.py` `_resolve_spell` | sos_1, sos_120 |\n178\t| 5 | Know how much mana a spell cost | In `cast_spell`, immediately after `player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)`, set `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc`. (X-cost spells undercount X; acceptable — none of these targets are X spells.) | `engine/casting.py` | sos_57 |\n179\t| 6 | Planeswalker dies at 0 loyalty | Add `_sba_planeswalker_zero_loyalty(game)`: for each battlefield permanent with `CardType.PLANESWALKER` and `loyalty <= 0`, move it to its owner's graveyard via `_move_to_graveyard` (or a `PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent`). Call it inside `check_state_based_actions`. | `engine/state_based_actions.py` | sos_97 |\n180\t| 7 | \"Target opponent skips their next X turns\" | Add `self.skipped_turns: dict[int, int] = {}` in `GameState.__init__`. In `advance_phase`'s end-of-turn branch, after computing the candidate `active_player_index`, loop: while `self.skipped_turns.get(candidate, 0) > 0`, decrement it and advance the **normal** rotation again (`candidate = self._normal_next_index; self._normal_next_index = 1 - self._normal_next_index`); then commit `candidate`. Card code does `game.skipped_turns[opp_idx] = game.skipped_turns.get(opp_idx, 0) + X`. (Interaction with `extra_turns` is out of scope, matching the existing documented `extra_turns` limitation.) | `engine/game_state.py` `advance_phase` | sos_97 |\n181\t| 8 | A permanent grants cost reduction to *other* spells you cast | In `get_cost_reduction`, after `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, add: for each `obj` in `game.get_battlefield(controller).get_all()`, if it has `grants_cost_reduction`, `raw += obj.grants_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)`. Then clamp as today. | `engine/casting.py` `get_cost_reduction` | sos_245 |\n182\t\n183\t**No engine change needed for:** Converge (read `card.colors_spent`), Miracle\n184\t(`DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` + manual `{2}` payment + `cast_spell_free`), coin flips\n185\t(route each flip through `controller.choose_yes_no(...)` so tests can script\n186\theads/tails), \"each opponent's upkeep\" (condition reads `game.active_player`),\n187\trestricted mana (\"spend only on instant/sorcery\") — **not modeled**, the FDN\n188\treference `fdn_141` deliberately ignores the same restriction, so you ignore it too.\n189\t\n190\t---\n191\t\n192\t## SECTION 2 — Per-card plans\n193\t\n194\t### sos_4 — Together as One  ({6} Sorcery, Converge)  — *start here*\n195\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, [this] deals X\n196\t  damage to any target, and you gain X life, where X = number of colors of mana\n197\t  spent to cast this spell.\"\n198\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_205` (Wardens of the Cycle) — Converge via\n199\t  `colors_spent`. Damage/target pattern: `cards/fdn/fdn_13`.\n200\t- **Seams:** subclass `Sorcery`, `{6}` cost. `get_targets` returns **two**\n201\t  `TargetRequirement`s: `[0]` a player (zone `BATTLEFIELD` is fine; filter\n202\t  `hasattr(obj,\"life\")`), `[1]` \"any target\" (creature or player —\n203\t  `filter_fn` accepts a player or a battlefield creature). `on_resolve`: read\n204\t  `self.chosen_targets`; compute `cs = getattr(self, \"colors_spent\", 0); X =\n205\t  len(cs) if isinstance(cs, (list, set, tuple)) else int(cs)`; then `draw_card` X\n206\t  times for target player, `deal_damage(game, self, any_target, X)`, and\n207\t  `self.controller.life += X`.\n208\t- **Engine change:** none. (`cast_spell` already records `colors_spent`.)\n209\t- **Edge cases to test:** X=0 (all-generic payment → no draws/damage/life); X via\n210\t  multi-color mana pool (set `mana={WHITE:1,BLUE:1,BLACK:1,...}` then cast and\n211\t  assert draws == distinct colors); damage to a creature vs to a player; following\n212\t  `fdn_205`'s test convention you can also set `card.colors_spent = 3` directly and\n213\t  call `on_resolve`.\n214\t\n215\t### sos_57 — Mana Sculpt  ({1}{U}{U} Instant)  — needs gaps #3, #5\n216\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount\n217\t  of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of\n218\t  your next main phase.\"\n219\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (Refute) — counter-target-spell pattern\n220\t  (`can_cast` requires a spell on the stack, `get_targets` with `zone=Zone.STACK`,\n221\t  the `_counter_spell` helper that pops the `StackObject` and moves its source card\n222\t  to the graveyard). You may copy that helper into this card module.\n223\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Instant`. On resolve: counter the target (reuse\n224\t  Refute's helper). Read the countered card's `mana_spent` (set by **gap #5** when\n225\t  it was cast). If `self.controller` controls a permanent with `\"Wizard\"` in\n226\t  `subtypes`, register a **one-shot** delayed trigger on\n227\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (**gap #3**): condition `event.player is\n228\t  controller`; effect adds `mana_spent` `{C}` to the controller's pool\n229\t  (`controller.mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, n)`) and then\n230\t  `game.trigger_manager.unregister(self)` so it fires only once. Register with\n231\t  `source=self`, `controller=self.controller`.\n232\t- **Edge cases:** countering an opponent's {3}{R}{R}-style spell → 5 `{C}` next\n233\t  main phase; no Wizard → no mana scheduled; the delayed mana appears at the\n234\t  controller's *next* main phase only once (not every turn); target spell already\n235\t  gone (fizzles cleanly). Test the delayed trigger by registering it then\n236\t  firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller, is_first=True)`\n237\t  via `game.trigger_manager.fire_event` and resolving.\n238\t\n239\t### sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant  ({2}{W}{B}, 4/4 Dragon, Flying/Vigilance)  — needs gap #2\n240\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"Flying, vigilance. Each instant and sorcery spell you cast\n241\t  has casualty 1. (As you cast it, you may sacrifice a creature with power ≥1. When\n242\t  you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.)\"\n243\t- **FDN analogue:** condition→effect capture pattern `cards/fdn/fdn_141`; spell\n244\t  copying via `engine/stack.py` `copy_spell(game, original_stackobj, controller,\n245\t  new_targets=None)`.\n246\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING |\n247\t  Keyword.VIGILANCE`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`. In\n248\t  `register_triggers` register a trigger on `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (**gap #2**):\n249\t  condition fires only when `event.controller is <Silverquill's controller>` and\n250\t  `event.card` is an instant/sorcery and `event.card is not self`; capture\n251\t  `event.spell` (the `StackObject`) into a closure `deque` and return `True`.\n252\t  Effect: pop the `StackObject`; ask the controller `choose_yes_no(\"Pay casualty —\n253\t  sacrifice a creature with power ≥1?\")`; if yes, have them `choose_card`/`choose`\n254\t  a controlled creature with `power >= 1`, `sacrifice(game, controller, creature)`,\n255\t  then `copy = copy_spell(game, stack_obj, controller); game.stack.push(copy)`.\n256\t- **Edge cases:** casting a creature spell → no casualty (filter on inst/sorc);\n257\t  declining the sacrifice; no legal (power ≥1) creature to sac; the copy resolves\n258\t  before the original (it's pushed above); copy with same targets (default).\n259\t  Because `cast_spell` resolves immediately in `test_utils.cast_spell`, to observe\n260\t  the trigger you may need to drive the stack manually (`engine.casting.cast_spell`\n261\t  then `priority_loop`) — script the sacrifice choices.\n262\t\n263\t### sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer  ({6}{B}{G}, 5/5 Dragon, Flying/Deathtouch)  — needs gap #8\n264\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"Affinity for creatures (this spell costs {1} less per\n265\t  creature you control). Flying, deathtouch. Instant and sorcery spells you cast\n266\t  have affinity for creatures.\"\n267\t- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_6` (Claws Out, `cost_reduction` counting a\n268\t  subtype you control) and `cards/fdn/fdn_167` (counting via `cost_reduction`).\n269\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Creature`, `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`,\n270\t  legendary. (a) Its own affinity: `cost_reduction(game)` returns the number of\n271\t  creatures `self.controller` controls (count battlefield objects with\n272\t  `CardType.CREATURE`). (b) Granting affinity to your instant/sorcery spells: add a\n273\t  method `grants_cost_reduction(self, game, spell, controller) -> int` that returns\n274\t  the creature count **only when** `controller is self.controller` and `spell` has\n275\t  `CardType.INSTANT` or `CardType.SORCERY`; this is summed in by **gap #8**.\n276\t- **Edge cases:** Witherbloom's own cost drops by creature count (but not below the\n277\t  colored pips — `cost_reduction` only reduces generic, already clamped); an\n278\t  instant you cast while Witherbloom is out costs `{generic - creatures}`; a\n279\t  creature spell you cast is **not** reduced; when Witherbloom is not on the\n280\t  battlefield, no grant. Test by putting N creatures + Witherbloom on the\n281\t  battlefield, an instant in hand, and asserting `get_cost_reduction(game, instant,\n282\t  controller) == N` (don't count Witherbloom inconsistently — decide whether\n283\t  Witherbloom itself counts as a creature you control; per rules it does).\n284\t\n285\t### sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic  ({10}, 7/7 Avatar, Reach)  — needs gaps #1, #4\n286\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"This spell costs {1} less for each instant and sorcery card\n287\t  in your graveyard. Reach. Whenever this attacks, you may cast target instant or\n288\t  sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell\n289\t  would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n290\t- **FDN analogue:** cost reduction `cards/fdn/fdn_167`; attack-trigger + free-cast\n291\t  `cards/fdn/fdn_194` (Etali: registers `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, uses\n292\t  `cast_spell_free`).\n293\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Creature`, `{10}`, `Keyword.REACH`, legendary,\n294\t  `base_power/toughness=7`. `cost_reduction(game)` counts instant/sorcery cards in\n295\t  `self.controller`'s graveyard (verbatim `fdn_167`). `register_triggers`: register\n296\t  `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (**gap #1** makes it fire) with condition `event.creature\n297\t  is self`; effect: gather instant/sorcery cards in the controller's graveyard, let\n298\t  the controller choose one (`choose`/`choose_card`, \"you may\" via\n299\t  `choose_yes_no`), set `chosen._exile_on_resolve = True` (**gap #4** exiles it\n300\t  after it resolves), then `cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen,\n301\t  Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n302\t- **Edge cases:** cost reduction floor (can't reduce the `{10}` below 0; it's all\n303\t  generic so it can hit 0); attacking with an empty graveyard (no castable spell);\n304\t  the cast spell goes to **exile** not graveyard after resolving (assert it's in\n305\t  exile); declining the optional cast. After `declare_attackers`, the trigger sits\n306\t  on the stack — resolve it (`priority_loop`) and script the graveyard-card choice.\n307\t\n308\t### sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares  ({1}{W}{W}, 3/3 Cat Cleric, Prepared)\n309\t- **Oracle clauses (front):** \"When this enters, target player creates a 1/1 white\n310\t  and black Inkling token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures\n311\t  than you, this creature becomes prepared. (While prepared, you may cast a copy of\n312\t  its spell. Doing so unprepares it.)\" The spell half **Swords to Plowshares**\n313\t  ({W} Instant): \"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its\n314\t  power.\"\n315\t- **FDN analogue:** token creation `cards/fdn/fdn_148` (`create_token` with a\n316\t  `Creature` token, set `Keyword.FLYING`); exile + life via `engine/game.py`\n317\t  helpers.\n318\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Creature`, legendary, `{\"Cat\",\"Cleric\"}`,\n319\t  base 3/3. Do the ETB work in **`on_resolve`** (NOT a registered trigger — see the\n320\t  ETB-ordering note): choose a target player and `create_token` a 1/1 Inkling with\n321\t  flying for them; then count creatures — if an opponent controls more creatures\n322\t  than the controller, set `self._is_prepared = True`. Model \"cast a copy of its\n323\t  spell\" as an **activated ability** (`get_activated_abilities`) available only when\n324\t  `self._is_prepared`: its `effect` exiles a chosen target creature\n325\t  (`exile(game, target)`), gives that creature's controller life equal to its\n326\t  `power`, and sets `self._is_prepared = False`. (The engine has no split/adventure\n327\t  casting; this is the contained model. Document the simplification in a one-line\n328\t  comment.)\n329\t- **Edge cases:** prepared set only when opponent has strictly more creatures;\n330\t  token is 1/1, flying, owned by the chosen player; the STP half exiles and grants\n331\t  life = power (test with a 4/4 → +4 life to its controller); using the prepared\n332\t  ability flips `_is_prepared` back to `False`; ability unavailable when not\n333\t  prepared.\n334\t\n335\t### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian  ({3}{R}{W}, 5/5 Dragon, Flying/Haste)  — no engine gap\n336\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"Flying, haste. Each instant and sorcery card in your hand\n337\t  has miracle {2}. (You may cast it for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's\n338\t  the first card you drew this turn.) At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep,\n339\t  you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\"\n340\t- **FDN analogue:** loot (draw/discard) `cards/fdn/fdn_48`; trigger registration\n341\t  `cards/fdn/fdn_141`.\n342\t- **Seams (no engine change):** subclass `Creature`, `Keyword.FLYING |\n343\t  Keyword.HASTE`, legendary, base 5/5. `register_triggers` registers two triggers:\n344\t  1. **Miracle** on `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`: condition — `event.player is\n345\t     <controller>`, `event.card` is an instant/sorcery, and it is the first card\n346\t     drawn this turn (`getattr(event.player, \"cards_drawn_this_turn\", 0) == 1`);\n347\t     capture `event.card`. Effect — if `controller.choose_yes_no(\"Cast for\n348\t     miracle {2}?\")` and `controller.mana_pool.can_pay(ManaCost(generic=2))`:\n349\t     `controller.mana_pool.pay(ManaCost(generic=2))` then\n350\t     `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.HAND)` (free-cast bypasses\n351\t     timing; the `{2}` is paid manually — this *is* the miracle cost).\n352\t  2. **Loot** on `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`: condition — `game.active_player\n353\t     is not <controller>` (an opponent's upkeep) and `controller` controls\n354\t     `self`. Effect — `if controller.choose_yes_no(\"Discard then draw?\")` and hand\n355\t     non-empty: `choose_card` → `discard` → `draw_card`.\n356\t- **Edge cases:** miracle only on the *first* draw of the turn (second draw of an\n357\t  inst/sorc does nothing); miracle on a non-inst/sorc draw does nothing; can't\n358\t  afford `{2}` → no cast; loot fires on the opponent's upkeep but not the\n359\t  controller's; declining the loot. Seed the library by mutating\n360\t  `zones[Zone.LIBRARY]` directly, then call `draw_card` to fire the miracle path.\n361\t\n362\t### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer  ({1}{B}{B} Legendary Planeswalker, loyalty 3)  — needs gaps #6, #7\n363\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"+1: Surveil 2. −1: Any number of target players each discard\n364\t  a card. −2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your\n365\t  graveyard to the battlefield. −7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their\n366\t  next X turns, where X = number of heads.\"\n367\t- **FDN analogues:** planeswalker shape `cards/fdn/fdn_134` (Ajani — subclass\n368\t  `Planeswalker`, set `starting_loyalty`, return `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost,\n369\t  effect, description)` list from `get_loyalty_abilities`, read targets via a\n370\t  `_resolve_target` backdoor or `controller.choose_*`); surveil `cards/fdn/fdn_157`\n371\t  (library top + `choose_yes_no`); reanimation `cards/fdn/fdn_187` (Zombify —\n372\t  `move_to_zone(game, target, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)`).\n373\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Planeswalker`, `starting_loyalty=3`,\n374\t  `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtype `{\"Ral\"}`, color black. `get_loyalty_abilities`\n375\t  returns four `LoyaltyAbility`s whose `effect(game)` callables (each selects its\n376\t  own targets at resolution via `controller.choose_*`, honoring an optional\n377\t  `self._resolve_target` backdoor like Ajani):\n378\t  - **+1 Surveil 2:** top two library cards, `choose_yes_no` each → graveyard or\n379\t    keep on top (verbatim `fdn_157`).\n380\t  - **−1 discard:** pick target player(s) (in 2-player, the opponent and/or self\n381\t    via `choose`/`choose_yes_no`); each chosen player `choose_card` →\n382\t    `discard(game, player, card)`.\n383\t  - **−2 reanimate:** filter the controller's graveyard to creature cards with\n384\t    `card.mana_cost.cmc <= 3`; `move_to_zone(target, Zone.GRAVEYARD,\n385\t    Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (verbatim `fdn_187` + the cmc filter).\n386\t  - **−7 skip turns:** five coin flips via `controller.choose_yes_no(\"Coin flip:\n387\t    heads?\")`; `X = number of True`; `opp_idx = game.players.index(opponent)`;\n388\t    `game.skipped_turns[opp_idx] = game.skipped_turns.get(opp_idx, 0) + X` (**gap\n389\t    #7**).\n390\t  - Loyalty costs must reduce `loyalty`; with **gap #6** Ral dies when loyalty hits\n391\t    0 (e.g. after −2 from 2, or starting-3 then −7 is illegal — `activate_ability`\n392\t    rejects it since `3 - 7 < 0`).\n393\t- **Test approach:** build a `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source=ral, controller=p,\n394\t  loyalty_cost=ab.loyalty_cost, effect=ab.effect)` from each `get_loyalty_abilities`\n395\t  entry and call `engine.abilities.activate_ability` (needs sorcery-speed timing:\n396\t  set phase to a main phase, empty stack, active player), then resolve the stack.\n397\t  Or call the `effect` directly after manually setting `loyalty`.\n398\t- **Edge cases:** once-per-turn loyalty restriction; −7 unaffordable at loyalty 3\n399\t  (raises `AbilityError`); −2 with no ≤3-cmc creature in graveyard; coin flips all\n400\t  tails → X=0 → no skip; skip actually removes the opponent's next turn(s) (run\n401\t  turns and assert active player). Test gap #7 by setting `skipped_turns` and\n402\t  driving `advance_phase` across a turn boundary.\n403\t\n404\t### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone  ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, Paradigm)  — needs gaps #3, #4  — *hardest, do last with sos_257*\n405\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile\n406\t  cards with total mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of them without\n407\t  paying their mana costs. Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve\n408\t  a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its\n409\t  mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\"\n410\t- **FDN analogue:** exile-top + free-cast `cards/fdn/fdn_194` (Etali).\n411\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Sorcery`. `on_resolve`: pop the controller's\n412\t  library top repeatedly (`zones[Zone.LIBRARY]`), `move_to_zone(card,\n413\t  Zone.LIBRARY, Zone.EXILE)`, accumulate `card.mana_cost.cmc`, stop once the\n414\t  running total `>= 4` (or library empties). For each exiled **nonland** card,\n415\t  offer `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)` gated on\n416\t  `choose_yes_no` (verbatim Etali loop). **Paradigm:** set\n417\t  `self._exile_on_resolve = True` (**gap #4**, so Capstone exiles itself instead of\n418\t  going to the graveyard), and register an ongoing trigger on\n419\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (**gap #3**) with `source=self`,\n420\t  condition `event.player is controller and event.is_first`; effect — optionally\n421\t  (`choose_yes_no`) cast a **copy** of the exiled Capstone for free. Implement the\n422\t  copy with a small local helper that mirrors `engine/stack.py copy_spell`: shallow\n423\t  `copy.copy(self)`, set `owner/controller`, build a `StackObject` whose\n424\t  `on_resolve` calls the copy's `on_resolve`, and push it (the copy is a one-shot\n425\t  effect, not a real card in a zone, so don't worry about its post-resolution zone).\n426\t- **Edge cases:** exiling stops exactly when cumulative cmc ≥ 4 (one big card can\n427\t  satisfy it alone); lands among the exiled cards aren't castable; Capstone ends in\n428\t  **exile** (assert), not graveyard; the Paradigm trigger only fires on the\n429\t  controller's **first** (precombat) main phase, repeatedly each turn; the recurring\n430\t  copy re-runs the exile-and-cast effect. Verify the trigger is registered after\n431\t  resolution, then fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller,\n432\t  is_first=True)` and resolve.\n433\t\n434\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land)  — needs gap #2  — *hardest, do last*\n435\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color.\n436\t  Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell. {5}: If this isn't a\n437\t  creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever you cast an instant or\n438\t  sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n439\t- **FDN analogue:** mana abilities + ignored mana restriction `cards/fdn/fdn_141`\n440\t  (Giada: `get_mana_abilities` returning `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced,\n441\t  description)`; the \"spend only on …\" restriction is **not modeled** there, so\n442\t  ignore it here too); EOT pump pattern `cards/fdn/fdn_6`.\n443\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Land`.\n444\t  - `get_mana_abilities()` returns two `ManaAbility`s: (1) `cost = tap_cost`,\n445\t    `mana_produced` adds `ManaType.COLORLESS` 1; (2) `cost` taps + pays 1 life\n446\t    (`controller.life -= 1`), `mana_produced` adds one mana of a color the\n447\t    controller chooses (`controller.choose`). Ignore the spend-restriction.\n448\t  - **Animation ({5}):** `get_activated_abilities()` returns an `ActivatedAbility`\n449\t    whose `cost` checks the land isn't already a creature and pays `{5}`\n450\t    (`controller.mana_pool.can_pay/pay(ManaCost(generic=5))`), and whose `effect`\n451\t    turns it into a creature **permanently**. Because `effect_manager.apply_all`\n452\t    calls `_reset_characteristics()` (which on a base `CardImpl` resets\n453\t    `card_types`/`keywords` to originals) the transformation must survive resets.\n454\t    Cleanest contained approach: set a flag `self._is_animated = True`; give this\n455\t    class the creature surface so the engine treats it as a creature **while\n456\t    animated** — define instance attrs (`base_power=2, base_toughness=4,\n457\t    modified_power, modified_toughness, damage_marked=0, plus_one_counters=0,\n458\t    minus_one_counters=0, is_attacking=False, is_blocking=False,\n459\t    summoning_sick=False`) and `power`/`toughness` properties (modified + counters)\n460\t    on the class; and **override `_reset_characteristics`** to call\n461\t    `super()._reset_characteristics()` then, if `self._is_animated`, re-add\n462\t    `CardType.CREATURE` + subtype `\"Wizard\"` and reset `modified_power/toughness`\n463\t    to 2/4. Do **not** predefine `base_power` before animation (so a non-animated\n464\t    land is not picked up as an attacker by `declare_attackers_step`, which gates on\n465\t    `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")`); set those attrs in the animation `effect`.\n466\t  - **Granted trigger:** the \"whenever you cast an instant or sorcery, +1/+0 EOT\"\n467\t    ability uses **gap #2** (`SpellCastTriggeredEvent`). Register it in\n468\t    `register_triggers` (fires on the land's ETB); condition — `self._is_animated`,\n469\t    `event.controller is self.controller`, `event.card` is inst/sorcery; effect —\n470\t    add an end-of-turn `ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS,\n471\t    sublayer=MODIFY_PT, duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN, apply=lambda g:\n472\t    setattr(self, \"modified_power\", self.modified_power + 1))` (mirror `fdn_6`).\n473\t- **This is the highest-risk card** — write thorough unit tests: produces {C};\n474\t  pays 1 life for any color (life drops by 1); `{5}` flips it to a 2/4 Wizard\n475\t  creature that is still a land (`CardType.LAND` and `CardType.CREATURE` both\n476\t  present); animation is idempotent across `effect_manager.apply_all()` /\n477\t  cleanup (call `apply_all` and assert it's still a 2/4 creature); the pump adds\n478\t  +1/+0 per inst/sorc cast and resets at end of turn; a **non-animated** land is\n479\t  not a legal attacker.\n480\t\n481\t---\n482\t\n483\t## SECTION 3 — Implementation order\n484\t\n485\tEngine changes are small and additive; landing them first de-risks the cards.\n486\tWithin each group, build the card, write its `tests.py`, and run `pytest` (confirm\n487\t`engine_tests/` + FDN tests stay green) before moving on.\n488\t\n489\t**Group 0 — Engine groundwork (do all first).** Land gaps #1–#8 from Section 1 in\n490\tone pass and run the full suite. They don't depend on each other and every one is a\n491\tfew lines. Rationale: cards below assume these seams exist; landing them together\n492\tlets you verify the regression suite once and then focus purely on card logic.\n493\t\n494\t**Group 1 — Converge warm-up (no new card dependencies).**\n495\t1. **sos_4 Together as One** — exercises the existing `colors_spent` seam end-to-end;\n496\t   smallest card and validates your multi-target + `create_game`/`set_board_state`\n497\t   test scaffolding. Rationale: simplest, no gap, builds confidence.\n498\t\n499\t**Group 2 — Cost-reduction family (reuse `cost_reduction` + gap #8).**\n500\t2. **sos_245 Witherbloom** — self-affinity (`cost_reduction`, like `fdn_6`/`fdn_167`)\n501\t   plus the `grants_cost_reduction` hook behind gap #8.\n502\t3. **sos_1 The Dawning Archaic** — same `cost_reduction` shape, then layers on the\n503\t   attack trigger (gap #1) + free-cast (`fdn_194`) + exile-on-resolve (gap #4).\n504\t   Rationale: do the simpler cost-reduction card first, then the one that also\n505\t   needs combat/exile seams.\n506\t\n507\t**Group 3 — Spell-cast trigger family (gap #2).**\n508\t4. **sos_226 Silverquill** — casualty: the cleanest consumer of `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n509\t   + `copy_spell` + the `fdn_141` capture pattern. Rationale: validates gap #2 and\n510\t   the capture pattern before the manland reuses them.\n511\t\n512\t**Group 4 — Main-phase trigger family (gap #3) + counter.**\n513\t5. **sos_57 Mana Sculpt** — counter (`fdn_48`) + one-shot main-phase delayed mana\n514\t   (gaps #3, #5). Rationale: introduces `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n515\t   consumption with the simpler one-shot case before sos_120's recurring case.\n516\t\n517\t**Group 5 — Standalone medium/expert (no gaps).**\n518\t6. **sos_13 Emeritus // Swords to Plowshares** — ETB token (`fdn_148`) + prepared +\n519\t   STP activated ability. No engine change.\n520\t7. **sos_201 Lorehold** — miracle (draw trigger + manual `{2}` + `cast_spell_free`)\n521\t   + opponent-upkeep loot. No engine change. Rationale: both are self-contained\n522\t   trigger cards; do them once the trigger/`cast_spell_free` patterns are familiar.\n523\t\n524\t**Group 6 — Planeswalker (gaps #6, #7).**\n525\t8. **sos_97 Ral Zarek** — four loyalty abilities reusing surveil (`fdn_157`),\n526\t   reanimation (`fdn_187`), discard, plus PW-death SBA (gap #6) and skip-turns\n527\t   (gap #7). Rationale: it reuses several earlier patterns and needs two dedicated\n528\t   gaps, so tackle it after those patterns are proven.\n529\t\n530\t**Group 7 — Hardest, do last.**\n531\t9. **sos_120 Improvisation Capstone** — exile-and-free-cast (`fdn_194`) + Paradigm\n532\t   recurring self-copy (gaps #3, #4). Reuses the main-phase event from sos_57 and\n533\t   the exile-on-resolve flag from sos_1, now in the harder recurring form.\n534\t10. **sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex** — manland: mana abilities + permanent\n535\t    animation through the layer/reset system + granted pump (gap #2). Highest risk\n536\t    because Land is not a `Creature`; do it last with the most test coverage.\n537\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f0f0606-b316-4229-9b01-03fec511ba77","uuid":"c8ac8ad0-03b1-4631-82c1-2fafcba503e7","timestamp":"2026-06-04T12:05:58.110Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN.md — SOS Implementation Plan (handoff to the implementer)\n\nYou are the implementation agent. This file is your **entire** brief — the planning\nsession that produced it is gone. Implement 10 SOS cards in\n`cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` (collector numbers **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201,\n226, 245, 257**), making **additive** engine changes as needed, and write your own\ntests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n\n## Hard constraints (from AGENTS.md — do not violate)\n\n1. **Card location invariant** — each card's class stays in\n   `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. The class names are fixed (already in the\n   stubs): `TheDawningArchaic`, `TogetherAsOne`,\n   `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares`, `ManaSculpt`, `RalZarekGuestLecturer`,\n   `ImprovisationCapstone`, `LoreholdTheHistorian`, `SilverquillTheDisputant`,\n   `WitherbloomTheBalancer`, `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex`.\n2. **Read-only tests** — never edit/add/delete anything in `engine_tests/`, and\n   never edit existing `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`. Read them as examples only.\n3. **Additive-only engine** — you MAY add files/methods/classes/helpers in\n   `engine/` and MAY modify the **bodies** of existing functions. You MUST NOT\n   rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/`. No\n   refactoring. After every engine change, run `pytest` and confirm\n   `engine_tests/` and all FDN tests still pass.\n4. Rules questions → grep `RULEBOOK.txt` (see `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n\n---\n\n## Engine facts you must know (verified against the source)\n\nThese are the seams the per-card plans rely on. File references are current.\n\n**Card hooks** (`engine/card.py`, base `CardImpl`): `can_cast(game)->bool`,\n`cost_reduction(game)->int` (generic-only reduction; clamped `0..generic`),\n`on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)`, `get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]`,\n`register_triggers(game)`, `register_replacement_effects(game)`,\n`get_activated_abilities()->list[ActivatedAbility]`, `get_modes()`. Subclasses:\n`Creature` (`base_power/base_toughness`, `modified_power/modified_toughness`,\n`power`/`toughness` properties = modified + `plus_one_counters` − `minus_one_counters`,\n`_reset_characteristics()`), `Instant`, `Sorcery`, `Enchantment`, `Aura`,\n`Artifact`, `ArtifactCreature`, `Planeswalker` (`starting_loyalty`, `loyalty`,\n`get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]`), `Land` (`can_cast` returns\n`False`, `get_mana_abilities()->list[ManaAbility]`).\n\n**Targeting** (`engine/types.py`): `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)`.\nThe cast pipeline calls `player.choose_target` once per spec and stores results, in\norder, on `card.chosen_targets`. At resolution read them back. The FDN convention\n(see `cards/fdn/fdn_48`, `fdn_187`) is a module helper:\n```python\ndef _get_chosen_target(card, game):\n    chosen = getattr(card, \"chosen_targets\", None)\n    if chosen: return chosen[0]\n    return getattr(card, \"_resolve_target\", None)  # test backdoor\n```\n\n**Casting** (`engine/casting.py`):\n- `cast_spell(game, player, card)` — full pipeline: timing → `can_cast` → hand →\n  stack → targets → protection → cost reduction → pay → records\n  `card.colors_spent = list(pool.last_payment_colors)` → `on_cast` → push\n  `StackObject`. **Does NOT currently fire a spell-cast event** (gap #2) and **does\n  NOT record total mana spent** (gap #5).\n- `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` — casts with **no timing and no\n  mana**, goes on the stack normally, can be countered. Used by Etali (`fdn_194`).\n- `_resolve_spell(...)` — calls `card.on_resolve`, then moves permanents →\n  battlefield, instants/sorceries → graveyard (no replacement consulted on this\n  move; see gap #4).\n- `get_cost_reduction(...)` only queries the card's own `cost_reduction` (gap #8).\n- `is_sorcery_speed(game, player)` exists. `ManaCost.cmc` = generic + pips + hybrids\n  (X counts as 0); `card.mana_cost.cmc` is a card's mana value.\n\n**Zones** (`engine/zones.py`): `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *,\nreplacement_event=None)`. Replacement effects are consulted **only when\n`replacement_event` is given AND `from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`**. On ETB it fires\n`EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` **before** calling the card's `register_triggers`\n/ `register_replacement_effects` (so a permanent's own ETB trigger does NOT catch\nits own entry — do \"when this enters\" work in `on_resolve` instead, like\n`fdn_157`/`fdn_205`). On leaving the battlefield it fires LTB / CreatureDies then\nunregisters the card's triggers/replacements.\n\n**Helpers** (`engine/game.py`): `draw_card(game, player)` (increments\n`player.cards_drawn_this_turn`, fires `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`),\n`discard(game, player, card)`, `create_token(game, player, token)`,\n`destroy(game, permanent)`, `exile(game, obj)`, `deal_damage(game, src, tgt, amt)`,\n`add_counter(game, permanent, counter_type, amount)` (supports `\"loyalty\"`,\n`\"+1/+1\"`), `sacrifice(game, player, permanent)`.\n\n**Triggers** (`engine/triggers.py`): `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition,\neffect, source, controller)`. `condition(game, event)->bool`; `effect(game)->None`\n— **the effect does NOT receive the event**. To pass data from condition to effect,\nuse the closure-queue pattern from `cards/fdn/fdn_141` (condition appends to a\n`deque`, returns `True`; effect `popleft()`s it). `fire_event` matches by\n`isinstance(event, event_type)` (subclass-aware), orders APNAP, pushes a\n`StackObject` per match. `unregister(source)` removes all triggers whose `source`\nis that object (identity) — use for one-shot delayed triggers.\n\n**Events** (`engine/events.py`): already-defined event classes you will use:\n`EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent, controller, ...)`,\n`DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card)`,\n`SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)` (defined; **never\nfired** — gap #2), `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)` (defined; **never\nfired** — gap #1), `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` (fired each upkeep, **no\nplayer field** — a condition must read `game.active_player`),\n`CreatureDiesTriggeredEvent`. Replacement events:\n`MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination, controller, owner, prevented)` with\nsubclasses `CreatureDiesReplacementEvent(creature)`,\n`PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent(permanent)`, `SacrificeReplacementEvent`;\n`.card` property resolves on the subclass. Pattern reference: `cards/fdn/fdn_244`.\n\n**Abilities** (`engine/abilities.py`): `activate_ability(game, player, ability)`\nwhere `ability` is `ActivatedAbilityInstance(source, controller, cost, effect,\nis_mana_ability, description)` or `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source, controller,\nloyalty_cost, effect, description)`. Loyalty: sorcery-speed only, once/turn (keyed\non `object_id`+`turn_number`), adjusts `source.loyalty`, pushes `effect` to the\nstack. `tap_cost(game, source)` taps if untapped. There is **no** auto-bridge from\n`LoyaltyAbility` (the dataclass returned by `get_loyalty_abilities`) to\n`LoyaltyAbilityInstance`; in tests, build the instance yourself from the\ndataclass's `loyalty_cost`/`effect` and call `activate_ability`, or construct a\n`LoyaltyAbilityInstance` directly.\n\n**Mana** (`engine/mana.py`): `pool.add(type, n)`, `pool.pay(cost)`,\n`pool.can_pay(cost)`, `pool.last_payment_colors` (sorted distinct `Color`s spent on\nthe most recent `pay`, colorless excluded). `ManaType` includes `COLORLESS`.\n\n**Turn loop** (`engine/turn.py` `run_turn`): fires only\n`BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` (upkeep). Main phases are `(phase, None)` and\ncurrently fire **no** begin-of-main event (gap #3). Combat steps dispatch to\n`engine/combat.py`. Cleanup runs `effect_manager.remove_expired` + `apply_all`,\nclears damage/combat flags, empties mana.\n\n**SBAs** (`engine/state_based_actions.py` `check_state_based_actions`): life≤0,\ntoughness≤0, lethal damage, empty-library draw, legend rule, tokens off battlefield,\nunattached auras, counter annihilation. **No planeswalker-0-loyalty check** (gap #6).\n\n**Continuous effects** (`engine/continuous_effects.py`):\n`ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)`;\n`Layer.{COPY,CONTROL,TEXT,TYPE,COLOR,ABILITY,POWER_TOUGHNESS}`,\n`SubLayer.{CHARACTERISTIC_DEFINING,SET_PT,MODIFY_PT,COUNTERS}`,\n`DURATION_PERMANENT=-1`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0`. `effect_manager.add(effect)`.\n`apply_all` first calls each battlefield object's `_reset_characteristics()` then\nre-applies effects in layer/timestamp order (so granted types/keywords/P-T must be\nmodeled as registered effects, or restored in an overridden\n`_reset_characteristics`, or they get wiped). EOT +X/+X pattern: `cards/fdn/fdn_6`.\n\n**Custom keywords are behavioral, not enum values.** `engine/types.py` `Keyword`\nhas only evergreen flags (FLYING, HASTE, VIGILANCE, DEATHTOUCH, REACH, TRAMPLE,\nPROWESS, WARD, …). **Converge, Prepared, Paradigm, Miracle, Casualty, Affinity do\nNOT exist as `Keyword` values and you do NOT need to add them** — implement them as\nbehavior (cost reduction / triggers / on_resolve). Only set the evergreen keywords\n(Reach, Flying, Haste, Vigilance, Deathtouch) via the `Keyword` flag. The FDN\nreferences confirm this (`fdn_6` Affinity, `fdn_205` Converge use no enum keyword).\n\n**Test helpers** (`test_utils.py`): `create_game(deck1, deck2, *, scripts=(s1,s2),\nplayer1_life, player2_life)` (players are `DeterministicPlayer`s);\n`set_board_state(game, idx, *, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana=)` —\n**note there is NO `library=` or `exile=` parameter**: to seed those zones, mutate\n`game.players[i].zones[Zone.LIBRARY]` / `[Zone.EXILE]` directly with `.add(card)`;\n`cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=)` (scripts targets, casts, resolves the whole\nstack); `advance_to_phase(game, phase, step=None)`; `declare_attackers(game,\n[names])` (calls `declare_attackers_step` then leaves triggers on the stack — you\nmust resolve them, e.g. `from engine.stack import priority_loop; priority_loop(game)`\nor pop manually); `declare_blockers`. `DeterministicPlayer._script` is a `deque`;\nscripted answers feed `choose`, `choose_target`, `choose_yes_no`, `choose_card`,\n`assign_damage_order` in pop order. Reset object ids between tests if needed with\n`GameObject.reset_id_counter()`.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 1 — Engine gaps table\n\nPrefer the *smallest* additive change. All eight are independent and small. Make\nthem first (see Section 3), then verify `engine_tests/` + FDN tests are green.\n\n| # | Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | \"Whenever ~ attacks\" triggers fire | In `declare_attackers_step`, after `attacker.is_attacking = True` and tapping, call `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))` for each declared attacker (import the event). | `engine/combat.py` `declare_attackers_step`; event already in `engine/events.py` | sos_1 |\n| 2 | \"Whenever you cast …\" / casualty triggers fire | At the end of `cast_spell` (after the `StackObject` is pushed) fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player)`. Do the same at the end of `cast_spell_free`. (Copies via `copy_spell` do NOT go through these, so no recursion.) | `engine/casting.py`; event already in `engine/events.py` | sos_226, sos_257 |\n| 3 | \"At the beginning of your … main phase\" triggers | Add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=None, is_first=False)` to `engine/events.py`. In `engine/turn.py` `run_turn`, add a branch: when `game.phase in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None`, fire it (before `priority_loop`) with `player=game.active_player`, `is_first=(game.phase == Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN)`. | `engine/events.py` + `engine/turn.py` | sos_57, sos_120 |\n| 4 | \"If it would go to your graveyard, exile it instead\" (for a resolving spell) | In `_resolve_spell`, the instant/sorcery branch: if `getattr(card, \"_exile_on_resolve\", False)` is set, `move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.EXILE)` instead of to graveyard. | `engine/casting.py` `_resolve_spell` | sos_1, sos_120 |\n| 5 | Know how much mana a spell cost | In `cast_spell`, immediately after `player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)`, set `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc`. (X-cost spells undercount X; acceptable — none of these targets are X spells.) | `engine/casting.py` | sos_57 |\n| 6 | Planeswalker dies at 0 loyalty | Add `_sba_planeswalker_zero_loyalty(game)`: for each battlefield permanent with `CardType.PLANESWALKER` and `loyalty <= 0`, move it to its owner's graveyard via `_move_to_graveyard` (or a `PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent`). Call it inside `check_state_based_actions`. | `engine/state_based_actions.py` | sos_97 |\n| 7 | \"Target opponent skips their next X turns\" | Add `self.skipped_turns: dict[int, int] = {}` in `GameState.__init__`. In `advance_phase`'s end-of-turn branch, after computing the candidate `active_player_index`, loop: while `self.skipped_turns.get(candidate, 0) > 0`, decrement it and advance the **normal** rotation again (`candidate = self._normal_next_index; self._normal_next_index = 1 - self._normal_next_index`); then commit `candidate`. Card code does `game.skipped_turns[opp_idx] = game.skipped_turns.get(opp_idx, 0) + X`. (Interaction with `extra_turns` is out of scope, matching the existing documented `extra_turns` limitation.) | `engine/game_state.py` `advance_phase` | sos_97 |\n| 8 | A permanent grants cost reduction to *other* spells you cast | In `get_cost_reduction`, after `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, add: for each `obj` in `game.get_battlefield(controller).get_all()`, if it has `grants_cost_reduction`, `raw += obj.grants_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)`. Then clamp as today. | `engine/casting.py` `get_cost_reduction` | sos_245 |\n\n**No engine change needed for:** Converge (read `card.colors_spent`), Miracle\n(`DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` + manual `{2}` payment + `cast_spell_free`), coin flips\n(route each flip through `controller.choose_yes_no(...)` so tests can script\nheads/tails), \"each opponent's upkeep\" (condition reads `game.active_player`),\nrestricted mana (\"spend only on instant/sorcery\") — **not modeled**, the FDN\nreference `fdn_141` deliberately ignores the same restriction, so you ignore it too.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 2 — Per-card plans\n\n### sos_4 — Together as One  ({6} Sorcery, Converge)  — *start here*\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, [this] deals X\n  damage to any target, and you gain X life, where X = number of colors of mana\n  spent to cast this spell.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_205` (Wardens of the Cycle) — Converge via\n  `colors_spent`. Damage/target pattern: `cards/fdn/fdn_13`.\n- **Seams:** subclass `Sorcery`, `{6}` cost. `get_targets` returns **two**\n  `TargetRequirement`s: `[0]` a player (zone `BATTLEFIELD` is fine; filter\n  `hasattr(obj,\"life\")`), `[1]` \"any target\" (creature or player —\n  `filter_fn` accepts a player or a battlefield creature). `on_resolve`: read\n  `self.chosen_targets`; compute `cs = getattr(self, \"colors_spent\", 0); X =\n  len(cs) if isinstance(cs, (list, set, tuple)) else int(cs)`; then `draw_card` X\n  times for target player, `deal_damage(game, self, any_target, X)`, and\n  `self.controller.life += X`.\n- **Engine change:** none. (`cast_spell` already records `colors_spent`.)\n- **Edge cases to test:** X=0 (all-generic payment → no draws/damage/life); X via\n  multi-color mana pool (set `mana={WHITE:1,BLUE:1,BLACK:1,...}` then cast and\n  assert draws == distinct colors); damage to a creature vs to a player; following\n  `fdn_205`'s test convention you can also set `card.colors_spent = 3` directly and\n  call `on_resolve`.\n\n### sos_57 — Mana Sculpt  ({1}{U}{U} Instant)  — needs gaps #3, #5\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount\n  of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of\n  your next main phase.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_48` (Refute) — counter-target-spell pattern\n  (`can_cast` requires a spell on the stack, `get_targets` with `zone=Zone.STACK`,\n  the `_counter_spell` helper that pops the `StackObject` and moves its source card\n  to the graveyard). You may copy that helper into this card module.\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Instant`. On resolve: counter the target (reuse\n  Refute's helper). Read the countered card's `mana_spent` (set by **gap #5** when\n  it was cast). If `self.controller` controls a permanent with `\"Wizard\"` in\n  `subtypes`, register a **one-shot** delayed trigger on\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (**gap #3**): condition `event.player is\n  controller`; effect adds `mana_spent` `{C}` to the controller's pool\n  (`controller.mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, n)`) and then\n  `game.trigger_manager.unregister(self)` so it fires only once. Register with\n  `source=self`, `controller=self.controller`.\n- **Edge cases:** countering an opponent's {3}{R}{R}-style spell → 5 `{C}` next\n  main phase; no Wizard → no mana scheduled; the delayed mana appears at the\n  controller's *next* main phase only once (not every turn); target spell already\n  gone (fizzles cleanly). Test the delayed trigger by registering it then\n  firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller, is_first=True)`\n  via `game.trigger_manager.fire_event` and resolving.\n\n### sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant  ({2}{W}{B}, 4/4 Dragon, Flying/Vigilance)  — needs gap #2\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"Flying, vigilance. Each instant and sorcery spell you cast\n  has casualty 1. (As you cast it, you may sacrifice a creature with power ≥1. When\n  you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.)\"\n- **FDN analogue:** condition→effect capture pattern `cards/fdn/fdn_141`; spell\n  copying via `engine/stack.py` `copy_spell(game, original_stackobj, controller,\n  new_targets=None)`.\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING |\n  Keyword.VIGILANCE`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`. In\n  `register_triggers` register a trigger on `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (**gap #2**):\n  condition fires only when `event.controller is <Silverquill's controller>` and\n  `event.card` is an instant/sorcery and `event.card is not self`; capture\n  `event.spell` (the `StackObject`) into a closure `deque` and return `True`.\n  Effect: pop the `StackObject`; ask the controller `choose_yes_no(\"Pay casualty —\n  sacrifice a creature with power ≥1?\")`; if yes, have them `choose_card`/`choose`\n  a controlled creature with `power >= 1`, `sacrifice(game, controller, creature)`,\n  then `copy = copy_spell(game, stack_obj, controller); game.stack.push(copy)`.\n- **Edge cases:** casting a creature spell → no casualty (filter on inst/sorc);\n  declining the sacrifice; no legal (power ≥1) creature to sac; the copy resolves\n  before the original (it's pushed above); copy with same targets (default).\n  Because `cast_spell` resolves immediately in `test_utils.cast_spell`, to observe\n  the trigger you may need to drive the stack manually (`engine.casting.cast_spell`\n  then `priority_loop`) — script the sacrifice choices.\n\n### sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer  ({6}{B}{G}, 5/5 Dragon, Flying/Deathtouch)  — needs gap #8\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"Affinity for creatures (this spell costs {1} less per\n  creature you control). Flying, deathtouch. Instant and sorcery spells you cast\n  have affinity for creatures.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_6` (Claws Out, `cost_reduction` counting a\n  subtype you control) and `cards/fdn/fdn_167` (counting via `cost_reduction`).\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Creature`, `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`,\n  legendary. (a) Its own affinity: `cost_reduction(game)` returns the number of\n  creatures `self.controller` controls (count battlefield objects with\n  `CardType.CREATURE`). (b) Granting affinity to your instant/sorcery spells: add a\n  method `grants_cost_reduction(self, game, spell, controller) -> int` that returns\n  the creature count **only when** `controller is self.controller` and `spell` has\n  `CardType.INSTANT` or `CardType.SORCERY`; this is summed in by **gap #8**.\n- **Edge cases:** Witherbloom's own cost drops by creature count (but not below the\n  colored pips — `cost_reduction` only reduces generic, already clamped); an\n  instant you cast while Witherbloom is out costs `{generic - creatures}`; a\n  creature spell you cast is **not** reduced; when Witherbloom is not on the\n  battlefield, no grant. Test by putting N creatures + Witherbloom on the\n  battlefield, an instant in hand, and asserting `get_cost_reduction(game, instant,\n  controller) == N` (don't count Witherbloom inconsistently — decide whether\n  Witherbloom itself counts as a creature you control; per rules it does).\n\n### sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic  ({10}, 7/7 Avatar, Reach)  — needs gaps #1, #4\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"This spell costs {1} less for each instant and sorcery card\n  in your graveyard. Reach. Whenever this attacks, you may cast target instant or\n  sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell\n  would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** cost reduction `cards/fdn/fdn_167`; attack-trigger + free-cast\n  `cards/fdn/fdn_194` (Etali: registers `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, uses\n  `cast_spell_free`).\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Creature`, `{10}`, `Keyword.REACH`, legendary,\n  `base_power/toughness=7`. `cost_reduction(game)` counts instant/sorcery cards in\n  `self.controller`'s graveyard (verbatim `fdn_167`). `register_triggers`: register\n  `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (**gap #1** makes it fire) with condition `event.creature\n  is self`; effect: gather instant/sorcery cards in the controller's graveyard, let\n  the controller choose one (`choose`/`choose_card`, \"you may\" via\n  `choose_yes_no`), set `chosen._exile_on_resolve = True` (**gap #4** exiles it\n  after it resolves), then `cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen,\n  Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n- **Edge cases:** cost reduction floor (can't reduce the `{10}` below 0; it's all\n  generic so it can hit 0); attacking with an empty graveyard (no castable spell);\n  the cast spell goes to **exile** not graveyard after resolving (assert it's in\n  exile); declining the optional cast. After `declare_attackers`, the trigger sits\n  on the stack — resolve it (`priority_loop`) and script the graveyard-card choice.\n\n### sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares  ({1}{W}{W}, 3/3 Cat Cleric, Prepared)\n- **Oracle clauses (front):** \"When this enters, target player creates a 1/1 white\n  and black Inkling token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures\n  than you, this creature becomes prepared. (While prepared, you may cast a copy of\n  its spell. Doing so unprepares it.)\" The spell half **Swords to Plowshares**\n  ({W} Instant): \"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its\n  power.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** token creation `cards/fdn/fdn_148` (`create_token` with a\n  `Creature` token, set `Keyword.FLYING`); exile + life via `engine/game.py`\n  helpers.\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Creature`, legendary, `{\"Cat\",\"Cleric\"}`,\n  base 3/3. Do the ETB work in **`on_resolve`** (NOT a registered trigger — see the\n  ETB-ordering note): choose a target player and `create_token` a 1/1 Inkling with\n  flying for them; then count creatures — if an opponent controls more creatures\n  than the controller, set `self._is_prepared = True`. Model \"cast a copy of its\n  spell\" as an **activated ability** (`get_activated_abilities`) available only when\n  `self._is_prepared`: its `effect` exiles a chosen target creature\n  (`exile(game, target)`), gives that creature's controller life equal to its\n  `power`, and sets `self._is_prepared = False`. (The engine has no split/adventure\n  casting; this is the contained model. Document the simplification in a one-line\n  comment.)\n- **Edge cases:** prepared set only when opponent has strictly more creatures;\n  token is 1/1, flying, owned by the chosen player; the STP half exiles and grants\n  life = power (test with a 4/4 → +4 life to its controller); using the prepared\n  ability flips `_is_prepared` back to `False`; ability unavailable when not\n  prepared.\n\n### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian  ({3}{R}{W}, 5/5 Dragon, Flying/Haste)  — no engine gap\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"Flying, haste. Each instant and sorcery card in your hand\n  has miracle {2}. (You may cast it for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's\n  the first card you drew this turn.) At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep,\n  you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** loot (draw/discard) `cards/fdn/fdn_48`; trigger registration\n  `cards/fdn/fdn_141`.\n- **Seams (no engine change):** subclass `Creature`, `Keyword.FLYING |\n  Keyword.HASTE`, legendary, base 5/5. `register_triggers` registers two triggers:\n  1. **Miracle** on `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`: condition — `event.player is\n     <controller>`, `event.card` is an instant/sorcery, and it is the first card\n     drawn this turn (`getattr(event.player, \"cards_drawn_this_turn\", 0) == 1`);\n     capture `event.card`. Effect — if `controller.choose_yes_no(\"Cast for\n     miracle {2}?\")` and `controller.mana_pool.can_pay(ManaCost(generic=2))`:\n     `controller.mana_pool.pay(ManaCost(generic=2))` then\n     `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.HAND)` (free-cast bypasses\n     timing; the `{2}` is paid manually — this *is* the miracle cost).\n  2. **Loot** on `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`: condition — `game.active_player\n     is not <controller>` (an opponent's upkeep) and `controller` controls\n     `self`. Effect — `if controller.choose_yes_no(\"Discard then draw?\")` and hand\n     non-empty: `choose_card` → `discard` → `draw_card`.\n- **Edge cases:** miracle only on the *first* draw of the turn (second draw of an\n  inst/sorc does nothing); miracle on a non-inst/sorc draw does nothing; can't\n  afford `{2}` → no cast; loot fires on the opponent's upkeep but not the\n  controller's; declining the loot. Seed the library by mutating\n  `zones[Zone.LIBRARY]` directly, then call `draw_card` to fire the miracle path.\n\n### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer  ({1}{B}{B} Legendary Planeswalker, loyalty 3)  — needs gaps #6, #7\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"+1: Surveil 2. −1: Any number of target players each discard\n  a card. −2: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your\n  graveyard to the battlefield. −7: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their\n  next X turns, where X = number of heads.\"\n- **FDN analogues:** planeswalker shape `cards/fdn/fdn_134` (Ajani — subclass\n  `Planeswalker`, set `starting_loyalty`, return `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost,\n  effect, description)` list from `get_loyalty_abilities`, read targets via a\n  `_resolve_target` backdoor or `controller.choose_*`); surveil `cards/fdn/fdn_157`\n  (library top + `choose_yes_no`); reanimation `cards/fdn/fdn_187` (Zombify —\n  `move_to_zone(game, target, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)`).\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Planeswalker`, `starting_loyalty=3`,\n  `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtype `{\"Ral\"}`, color black. `get_loyalty_abilities`\n  returns four `LoyaltyAbility`s whose `effect(game)` callables (each selects its\n  own targets at resolution via `controller.choose_*`, honoring an optional\n  `self._resolve_target` backdoor like Ajani):\n  - **+1 Surveil 2:** top two library cards, `choose_yes_no` each → graveyard or\n    keep on top (verbatim `fdn_157`).\n  - **−1 discard:** pick target player(s) (in 2-player, the opponent and/or self\n    via `choose`/`choose_yes_no`); each chosen player `choose_card` →\n    `discard(game, player, card)`.\n  - **−2 reanimate:** filter the controller's graveyard to creature cards with\n    `card.mana_cost.cmc <= 3`; `move_to_zone(target, Zone.GRAVEYARD,\n    Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` (verbatim `fdn_187` + the cmc filter).\n  - **−7 skip turns:** five coin flips via `controller.choose_yes_no(\"Coin flip:\n    heads?\")`; `X = number of True`; `opp_idx = game.players.index(opponent)`;\n    `game.skipped_turns[opp_idx] = game.skipped_turns.get(opp_idx, 0) + X` (**gap\n    #7**).\n  - Loyalty costs must reduce `loyalty`; with **gap #6** Ral dies when loyalty hits\n    0 (e.g. after −2 from 2, or starting-3 then −7 is illegal — `activate_ability`\n    rejects it since `3 - 7 < 0`).\n- **Test approach:** build a `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source=ral, controller=p,\n  loyalty_cost=ab.loyalty_cost, effect=ab.effect)` from each `get_loyalty_abilities`\n  entry and call `engine.abilities.activate_ability` (needs sorcery-speed timing:\n  set phase to a main phase, empty stack, active player), then resolve the stack.\n  Or call the `effect` directly after manually setting `loyalty`.\n- **Edge cases:** once-per-turn loyalty restriction; −7 unaffordable at loyalty 3\n  (raises `AbilityError`); −2 with no ≤3-cmc creature in graveyard; coin flips all\n  tails → X=0 → no skip; skip actually removes the opponent's next turn(s) (run\n  turns and assert active player). Test gap #7 by setting `skipped_turns` and\n  driving `advance_phase` across a turn boundary.\n\n### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone  ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, Paradigm)  — needs gaps #3, #4  — *hardest, do last with sos_257*\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile\n  cards with total mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of them without\n  paying their mana costs. Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve\n  a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its\n  mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\"\n- **FDN analogue:** exile-top + free-cast `cards/fdn/fdn_194` (Etali).\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Sorcery`. `on_resolve`: pop the controller's\n  library top repeatedly (`zones[Zone.LIBRARY]`), `move_to_zone(card,\n  Zone.LIBRARY, Zone.EXILE)`, accumulate `card.mana_cost.cmc`, stop once the\n  running total `>= 4` (or library empties). For each exiled **nonland** card,\n  offer `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)` gated on\n  `choose_yes_no` (verbatim Etali loop). **Paradigm:** set\n  `self._exile_on_resolve = True` (**gap #4**, so Capstone exiles itself instead of\n  going to the graveyard), and register an ongoing trigger on\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (**gap #3**) with `source=self`,\n  condition `event.player is controller and event.is_first`; effect — optionally\n  (`choose_yes_no`) cast a **copy** of the exiled Capstone for free. Implement the\n  copy with a small local helper that mirrors `engine/stack.py copy_spell`: shallow\n  `copy.copy(self)`, set `owner/controller`, build a `StackObject` whose\n  `on_resolve` calls the copy's `on_resolve`, and push it (the copy is a one-shot\n  effect, not a real card in a zone, so don't worry about its post-resolution zone).\n- **Edge cases:** exiling stops exactly when cumulative cmc ≥ 4 (one big card can\n  satisfy it alone); lands among the exiled cards aren't castable; Capstone ends in\n  **exile** (assert), not graveyard; the Paradigm trigger only fires on the\n  controller's **first** (precombat) main phase, repeatedly each turn; the recurring\n  copy re-runs the exile-and-cast effect. Verify the trigger is registered after\n  resolution, then fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller,\n  is_first=True)` and resolve.\n\n### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land)  — needs gap #2  — *hardest, do last*\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color.\n  Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell. {5}: If this isn't a\n  creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever you cast an instant or\n  sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** mana abilities + ignored mana restriction `cards/fdn/fdn_141`\n  (Giada: `get_mana_abilities` returning `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced,\n  description)`; the \"spend only on …\" restriction is **not modeled** there, so\n  ignore it here too); EOT pump pattern `cards/fdn/fdn_6`.\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Land`.\n  - `get_mana_abilities()` returns two `ManaAbility`s: (1) `cost = tap_cost`,\n    `mana_produced` adds `ManaType.COLORLESS` 1; (2) `cost` taps + pays 1 life\n    (`controller.life -= 1`), `mana_produced` adds one mana of a color the\n    controller chooses (`controller.choose`). Ignore the spend-restriction.\n  - **Animation ({5}):** `get_activated_abilities()` returns an `ActivatedAbility`\n    whose `cost` checks the land isn't already a creature and pays `{5}`\n    (`controller.mana_pool.can_pay/pay(ManaCost(generic=5))`), and whose `effect`\n    turns it into a creature **permanently**. Because `effect_manager.apply_all`\n    calls `_reset_characteristics()` (which on a base `CardImpl` resets\n    `card_types`/`keywords` to originals) the transformation must survive resets.\n    Cleanest contained approach: set a flag `self._is_animated = True`; give this\n    class the creature surface so the engine treats it as a creature **while\n    animated** — define instance attrs (`base_power=2, base_toughness=4,\n    modified_power, modified_toughness, damage_marked=0, plus_one_counters=0,\n    minus_one_counters=0, is_attacking=False, is_blocking=False,\n    summoning_sick=False`) and `power`/`toughness` properties (modified + counters)\n    on the class; and **override `_reset_characteristics`** to call\n    `super()._reset_characteristics()` then, if `self._is_animated`, re-add\n    `CardType.CREATURE` + subtype `\"Wizard\"` and reset `modified_power/toughness`\n    to 2/4. Do **not** predefine `base_power` before animation (so a non-animated\n    land is not picked up as an attacker by `declare_attackers_step`, which gates on\n    `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")`); set those attrs in the animation `effect`.\n  - **Granted trigger:** the \"whenever you cast an instant or sorcery, +1/+0 EOT\"\n    ability uses **gap #2** (`SpellCastTriggeredEvent`). Register it in\n    `register_triggers` (fires on the land's ETB); condition — `self._is_animated`,\n    `event.controller is self.controller`, `event.card` is inst/sorcery; effect —\n    add an end-of-turn `ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS,\n    sublayer=MODIFY_PT, duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN, apply=lambda g:\n    setattr(self, \"modified_power\", self.modified_power + 1))` (mirror `fdn_6`).\n- **This is the highest-risk card** — write thorough unit tests: produces {C};\n  pays 1 life for any color (life drops by 1); `{5}` flips it to a 2/4 Wizard\n  creature that is still a land (`CardType.LAND` and `CardType.CREATURE` both\n  present); animation is idempotent across `effect_manager.apply_all()` /\n  cleanup (call `apply_all` and assert it's still a 2/4 creature); the pump adds\n  +1/+0 per inst/sorc cast and resets at end of turn; a **non-animated** land is\n  not a legal attacker.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3 — Implementation order\n\nEngine changes are small and additive; landing them first de-risks the cards.\nWithin each group, build the card, write its `tests.py`, and run `pytest` (confirm\n`engine_tests/` + FDN tests stay green) before moving on.\n\n**Group 0 — Engine groundwork (do all first).** Land gaps #1–#8 from Section 1 in\none pass and run the full suite. They don't depend on each other and every one is a\nfew lines. Rationale: cards below assume these seams exist; landing them together\nlets you verify the regression suite once and then focus purely on card logic.\n\n**Group 1 — Converge warm-up (no new card dependencies).**\n1. **sos_4 Together as One** — exercises the existing `colors_spent` seam end-to-end;\n   smallest card and validates your multi-target + `create_game`/`set_board_state`\n   test scaffolding. Rationale: simplest, no gap, builds confidence.\n\n**Group 2 — Cost-reduction family (reuse `cost_reduction` + gap #8).**\n2. **sos_245 Witherbloom** — self-affinity (`cost_reduction`, like `fdn_6`/`fdn_167`)\n   plus the `grants_cost_reduction` hook behind gap #8.\n3. **sos_1 The Dawning Archaic** — same `cost_reduction` shape, then layers on the\n   attack trigger (gap #1) + free-cast (`fdn_194`) + exile-on-resolve (gap #4).\n   Rationale: do the simpler cost-reduction card first, then the one that also\n   needs combat/exile seams.\n\n**Group 3 — Spell-cast trigger family (gap #2).**\n4. **sos_226 Silverquill** — casualty: the cleanest consumer of `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`\n   + `copy_spell` + the `fdn_141` capture pattern. Rationale: validates gap #2 and\n   the capture pattern before the manland reuses them.\n\n**Group 4 — Main-phase trigger family (gap #3) + counter.**\n5. **sos_57 Mana Sculpt** — counter (`fdn_48`) + one-shot main-phase delayed mana\n   (gaps #3, #5). Rationale: introduces `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n   consumption with the simpler one-shot case before sos_120's recurring case.\n\n**Group 5 — Standalone medium/expert (no gaps).**\n6. **sos_13 Emeritus // Swords to Plowshares** — ETB token (`fdn_148`) + prepared +\n   STP activated ability. No engine change.\n7. **sos_201 Lorehold** — miracle (draw trigger + manual `{2}` + `cast_spell_free`)\n   + opponent-upkeep loot. No engine change. Rationale: both are self-contained\n   trigger cards; do them once the trigger/`cast_spell_free` patterns are familiar.\n\n**Group 6 — Planeswalker (gaps #6, #7).**\n8. **sos_97 Ral Zarek** — four loyalty abilities reusing surveil (`fdn_157`),\n   reanimation (`fdn_187`), discard, plus PW-death SBA (gap #6) and skip-turns\n   (gap #7). Rationale: it reuses several earlier patterns and needs two dedicated\n   gaps, so tackle it after those patterns are proven.\n\n**Group 7 — Hardest, do last.**\n9. **sos_120 Improvisation Capstone** — exile-and-free-cast (`fdn_194`) + Paradigm\n   recurring self-copy (gaps #3, #4). Reuses the main-phase event from sos_57 and\n   the exile-on-resolve flag from sos_1, now in the harder recurring form.\n10. **sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex** — manland: mana abilities + permanent\n    animation through the layer/reset system + granted pump (gap #2). Highest risk\n    because Land is not a `Creature`; do it last with the most test coverage.\n","numLines":537,"startLine":1,"totalLines":537}}}
